  ('10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000071', 'f0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000143', '[Q143] The escape velocity from the surface of Earth is $11.2$ km/s. If a planet has twice the mass and twice the radius of Earth, its escape velocity is:', 'MCQ', 4, 0, '[{"key":"A","text":"$22.4$ km/s"},{"key":"B","text":"$11.2$ km/s"},{"key":"C","text":"$5.6$ km/s"},{"key":"D","text":"$15.8$ km/s"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"B","key":"B"}'::jsonb, NULL),
  ('10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000072', 'f0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000146', '[Q146] A wire of resistance $16 \; \Omega$ is stretched uniformly to twice its original length. The new resistance of the wire will be:', 'MCQ', 4, 0, '[{"key":"A","text":"$32 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"B","text":"$16 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"C","text":"$64 \\; \\Omega$"},{"key":"D","text":"$8 \\; \\Omega$"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"C","key":"C"}'::jsonb, NULL),
  ('10000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000073', 'f0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000007', '58aeea98-85ee-4405-9225-57a9bf025aec', 'e0000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000149', '[Q149] In Young’s double-slit experiment, if the distance between the slits is halved and the screen distance is doubled, the fringe width becomes:', 'MCQ', 4, 0, '[{"key":"A","text":"$2$ times"},{"key":"B","text":"Halved"},{"key":"C","text":"Unchanged"},{"key":"D","text":"$4$ times"}]'::jsonb, '{"correct":"D","key":"D"}'::jsonb, NULL),
